.nh
.TH "TUSK" "1" "Jul 2026" "Tusk" "Tusk Manual"

.SH NAME
tusk-context - Compose a warm-context digest from the manifest [context] block


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtusk context [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the composed warm-context digest for this workspace.

.PP
The digest is the single entry point an agent calls at session start instead
of issuing three to five exploratory list/get/query calls. It returns:
.IP \(bu 2
Pinned nodes ([context.pinned]) with body + edges expanded by default.
.IP \(bu 2
Recent activity ([context.recent] or \fBrecent = "<alias>"\fR): one
alias result, typically a node list filtered with \fBmodified-since:<N>d\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Aliases ([context.include]): a fan-out over named, manifest-declared
aliases; each result is folded under its alias name.

.PP
Use --include to override the per-node expansion set for the pinned and
recent sections (default: body,edges). By default the digest prints in
its compact form; pass --json (or --format json) to emit JSON for piping
into another tool.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: compact|json (default: compact digest; use --json to emit JSON)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for context

.PP
\fB--include\fP=[]
	per-node include set for pinned + recent (default body,edges)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit structured JSON (sugar for --format json)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	emit debug-level logs to stderr


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Pull the digest at session start
  tusk context

  # Trim per-node payload to edges only
  tusk context --include edges

  # Pipe the digest into another tool
  tusk context --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtusk(1)\fP
